The example in the nest form:
RosettaCode(rocks(code, comparison, wiki), mocks(trolling))

... to the indent form:
0 RosettaCode
1 rocks
2 code
2 comparison
2 wiki
1 mocks
2 trolling

... drawn, four spaces a level:
RosettaCode
    rocks
        code
        comparison
        wiki
    mocks
        trolling

... back to the nest form:
RosettaCode(rocks(code, comparison, wiki), mocks(trolling))

The first and the final nest forms are the same: true
Each text read back is the form it was written from: true and true

Another tree: a(b(c(d, e), f), g, h(i(j(k)))), drawn:
a
    b
        c
            d
            e
        f
    g
    h
        i
            j
                k
Back from its indent form: a(b(c(d, e), f), g, h(i(j(k)))), the same: true
